{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58837","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69376","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-58838","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69377","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-69378","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-69379","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-69380","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-69381","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-69382","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-58839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69383","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58840","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69384","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-58841","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69385","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-69386","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-69387","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-58842","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69388","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-69389","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-58843","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69390","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-69391","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-69392","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-58844","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-58845","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69393","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58846","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69394","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-58847","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-58848","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69395","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58849","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69396","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-58850","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69397","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-58851","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69398","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-58852","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69399","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-69400","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-69401","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-58853","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69402","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-58855","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58858","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69403","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-58857","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58860","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69404","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-58859","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69405","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-58861","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58863","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69406","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-58864","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58866","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69407","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-69408","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-69409","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-58865","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58868","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69410","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-69411","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-58867","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69412","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-58869","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69413","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-58871","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69414","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-58873","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69415","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-58875","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69416","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58878","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69417","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-58879","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69418","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-69419","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-69420","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-58880","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-58881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69421","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58882","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69422","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-58883","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69423","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-58884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69424","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-69425","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-69426","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-69427","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-69428","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58885","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58887","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69429","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-69430","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-69431","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69432","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-69433","text":", "},{"id":"spn-69434","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-69435","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-58886","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69436","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-58888","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69437","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-69438","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-69439","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-58890","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69440","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-69441","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-69442","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-58892","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58895","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69443","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-69444","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-69445","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-69446","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-58894","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69447","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-69448","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-69449","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-69450","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-69451","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58897","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58899","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69452","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-58898","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69453","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-58900","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58903","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69454","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-58902","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69455","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-69456","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-69457","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-69458","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-69459","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58905","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58907","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69460","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-69461","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-58906","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69462","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-69463","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-58908","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58910","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69464","text":"4. "},{"id":"spn-69465","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-69466","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]},{"id":"blk-58911","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-69467","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-58912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69468","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-58913","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69469","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-69470","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-69471","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-69472","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-69473","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-58914","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69474","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-69475","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-69476","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-69477","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-58915","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58918","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69478","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-69479","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-69480","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-58917","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69481","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-69482","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-69483","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-69484","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-58919","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69485","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-69486","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-69487","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-69488","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-58921","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69489","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-69490","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-58923","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69491","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-69492","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-58925","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58928","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69493","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-69494","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-58927","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69495","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-69496","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-58929","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69497","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-69498","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-58931","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58934","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69499","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-69500","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-58933","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58936","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69501","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-69502","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-69503","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-58935","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69504","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-69505","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-69506","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-58937","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58940","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69507","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-69508","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-69509","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-58939","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58941","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69510","text":"2. "},{"id":"spn-69511","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]},{"id":"blk-58942","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58944","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69512","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-69513","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-58943","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58946","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69514","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-69515","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-58945","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58948","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69516","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-69517","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-58947","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58950","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69518","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-58949","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58951","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-69519","text":"3. "},{"id":"spn-69520","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-69521","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agentelic or the user's own API key) processes. SpecPrompt is a tool, not an agent. The MCP server version ("},{"id":"spn-69522","marks":["code"],"text":"spec_test_compile"},{"id":"spn-69523","text":") returns the prompt for the agent t